<title>USA: N.Y. board approves LILCO takeover, bonds.</title>
<headline>N.Y. board approves LILCO takeover, bonds.</headline>
<dateline>ALBANY, N.Y. 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York State Public Authorities Control Board Wednesday approved a plan for the Long Island Power Authority to takeover the Long Island Lighting Co's transmission and distribution system.</p>
<p>In a unanimous vote, the agency's move also authorizes LIPA to takeover LILCO's 18 percent share in the Nine Mile 2 nuclear plant. The deal envisions the sale of about $7.3 billion of tax-exempt bonds by LIPA.</p>
</text>
